WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:03.860 --> 00:04.560
There it is!

00:05.570 --> 00:07.630
We're finally at the Kalos League!

00:09.870 --> 00:15.300
Having got eight badges, Satoshi has come to the Kalos League, which will be held in Miare City.

00:16.080 --> 00:20.020
Satoshi's biggest challenge is about to begin!

00:21.370 --> 00:24.750
All of Miare City here is infected with the Kalos League fever,

00:25.080 --> 00:29.610
and excitement is in the air thanks to all the fans eagerly awaiting the start of the tournament.

00:30.250 --> 00:34.130
I'm Pachira, who will be reporting from the Kalos League here.

00:34.690 --> 00:39.140
I'm planning to do on-the-spot interviews with participating Trainers right away!

00:41.630 --> 00:44.060
Working as a television crew is too hard...

00:44.450 --> 00:47.960
But there's bound to be opportunities for us to get some Pokémon.

00:48.260 --> 00:50.400
After all, there should be strong Pokémon here.

00:50.750 --> 00:52.750
Let's look for an opportunity while doing this part-time job!

00:53.080 --> 00:55.070
We'll get both funds <i>and</i> Pokémon!

00:57.440 --> 00:58.890
Pull yourself together!

01:01.580 --> 01:03.540
Whoa, it's huge!

01:03.540 --> 01:04.680
There are so many people!

01:05.570 --> 01:07.130
We have finally made it here...

01:07.660 --> 01:09.770
So this is where you'll fight your decisive battles, Satoshi.

01:10.240 --> 01:10.720
Yeah.

01:11.110 --> 01:13.670
Strong Pokémon and strong Trainers will gather here.

01:14.320 --> 01:16.620
That alone makes us excited, right, Pikachu?

01:18.390 --> 01:19.480
Excuse me!

01:20.560 --> 01:22.680
Are you a Kalos League participant?

01:23.250 --> 01:24.190
Y-Yes.

01:24.570 --> 01:25.900
I'd like to have an interview.

01:26.150 --> 01:27.400
Huh? A-An interview?

01:28.030 --> 01:28.250
Gulp!

01:29.040 --> 01:30.450
It's the brat boy.

01:30.450 --> 01:31.650
We ran into him right away.

01:32.580 --> 01:33.530
Roll camera.

01:34.940 --> 01:35.630
Your name, please.

01:36.110 --> 01:38.210
Uh, I'm Satoshi from Masara Town.

01:38.920 --> 01:40.490
A word on your ambitions for this tournament, please.

01:41.060 --> 01:41.440
Okay.

01:41.940 --> 01:43.200
I am, of course, aiming to win the entire thing!

01:43.920 --> 01:45.540
I'll win, win and keep winning!

01:46.120 --> 01:47.500
I'll win the league, no matter what!

01:48.830 --> 01:49.730
Now I've said it, huh...?

01:51.400 --> 01:53.550
There is our declaration of victory!

01:53.880 --> 01:55.130
Please do your best!

01:55.130 --> 01:56.270
Thank you very much.

02:02.210 --> 02:07.970
The Kalos League Begins!
Mega Lizardon Showdown: X VS Y!!

02:08.560 --> 02:09.830
Satoshi, hurry!

02:08.970 --> 02:18.870
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:08.970 --> 02:18.870
Z

02:10.120 --> 02:12.000
You'll end up not making it in time to register!

02:12.390 --> 02:14.580
A lot of people were rooting for me, so I couldn't help it...

02:15.110 --> 02:16.030
Wait a second!

02:16.740 --> 02:20.440
Why don't you show me how strong the guy who declared to win <i>really</i> is?

02:20.990 --> 02:21.280
Huh?

02:21.780 --> 02:23.240
Let's have a battle!

02:25.740 --> 02:27.150
Wow, a Trimmien!

02:27.530 --> 02:28.690
You come just at the right moment.

02:29.020 --> 02:29.870
Before the League I wanted to...

02:30.360 --> 02:33.240
No, no, Satoshi! You don't have time!

02:33.240 --> 02:33.880
Okay...

02:34.320 --> 02:37.880
I am sorry. The registration deadline for the participants is very soon.

02:39.080 --> 02:39.920
Excuse us.

02:40.210 --> 02:41.160
Let's hurry!

02:41.550 --> 02:43.130
Sorry, another time, okay?

02:43.560 --> 02:46.280
What will you do if you don't make it in time and are unable to enter?

02:46.280 --> 02:48.200
Geez, you're such a child!

02:55.510 --> 02:56.640
Phew, we made it...

02:57.240 --> 02:58.990
Yeah, that was a close call.

03:00.900 --> 03:04.190
Everyone here has fought their way through their Gym matches, huh...?

03:05.340 --> 03:08.330
I'm already excited about how the battles will turn out.

03:14.480 --> 03:16.310
Shota, please watch us.

03:16.890 --> 03:18.420
I want to get my eighth badge...

03:19.130 --> 03:20.750
...and fight you at the League, no matter what.

03:21.350 --> 03:22.880
I can't leave it at that loss.

03:24.350 --> 03:25.920
Let's settle this at the League!

03:26.450 --> 03:28.140
Yes, of course!

03:33.940 --> 03:35.330
I knew he'd come.

03:36.350 --> 03:39.730
This is the Satoshi I have been chasing after.

03:43.350 --> 03:44.690
Satoshi, long time no see!

03:45.390 --> 03:46.240
Tierno!

03:46.430 --> 03:47.330
It has been a while.

03:47.570 --> 03:48.660
Oh, Trova!

03:48.660 --> 03:49.540
How're you doing?

03:49.540 --> 03:50.570
Fine, Eureka.

03:51.140 --> 03:53.800
Serena, I'm so happy to see you!

03:53.800 --> 03:54.620
Uh, same here.

03:55.100 --> 03:58.820
Trova and I watched the Tripokalon. You were amazing!

03:59.150 --> 03:59.920
Thank you.

04:00.290 --> 04:01.910
Well, I didn't become queen, though...

04:01.910 --> 04:02.590
Tch, tch, tch!

04:03.120 --> 04:04.910
You've become <i>my</i> queen, at least!

04:05.630 --> 04:07.210
Uhm... Huh? Where's Sana?

04:07.750 --> 04:09.170
She said she'd come later.

04:09.680 --> 04:10.410
I see.

04:11.220 --> 04:12.350
So you're both entering.

04:12.670 --> 04:13.250
Of course!

04:13.770 --> 04:15.200
The championship is mine!

04:15.780 --> 04:18.230
I will not hand it over so easily either!

04:18.890 --> 04:20.260
Me neither.

04:21.460 --> 04:21.650
Oh.

04:29.210 --> 04:30.750
It's Professor Platane and Alan...

04:34.060 --> 04:34.670
Alan!

04:37.450 --> 04:39.200
So you're gonna enter the Kalos League.

04:40.050 --> 04:40.410
Yeah.

04:41.140 --> 04:42.500
I wanted to fight you, after all.

04:43.160 --> 04:43.550
Me?

04:44.590 --> 04:46.520
And then there's the Mega Evolution energy.

04:46.940 --> 04:47.090
Huh?

04:47.740 --> 04:49.880
Nothing. I'll make sure to win my way up.

04:50.640 --> 04:51.840
So Satoshi, you make sure to win too.

04:52.700 --> 04:54.350
Okay, I won't lose!

04:54.820 --> 04:56.240
I'm aiming for league victory, after all!

05:03.700 --> 05:05.240
Sorry to keep you waiting!

05:05.800 --> 05:08.410
We will now reveal the brackets for the first round!

05:13.490 --> 05:15.740
The match-ups of the first round...

05:21.840 --> 05:23.250
...are as follows!

05:25.350 --> 05:27.170
So the first match is Trova against Alan, huh?

05:29.250 --> 05:31.170
Satoshi, you're in the second match.

05:31.530 --> 05:32.910
My opponent is...

05:38.690 --> 05:41.230
All right, I'm in the 23rd match!

05:44.080 --> 05:45.950
Everyone, please do your best!

05:48.410 --> 05:49.720
The opening battle, huh...?

05:50.420 --> 05:53.230
Trova, you'll be fine. After all, you've got a secret plan!

05:53.440 --> 05:54.970
Th-That is correct...

05:55.190 --> 05:55.430
What?

05:55.820 --> 05:57.770
What is it? Tell me!

05:57.770 --> 06:00.130
No. It is a surprise, after all.

06:00.580 --> 06:02.370
<i>You</i> will all be surprised as well.

06:02.990 --> 06:04.950
Come on! Why can't you tell me?

06:05.200 --> 06:06.350
Do you know what it is, Tierno?

06:06.350 --> 06:07.370
Uh, me?

06:07.370 --> 06:11.540
I want to keep it secret until tomorrow! After all, I might end up battling you, Satoshi!

06:20.030 --> 06:26.450
With weather so clear it almost seems like it wants to bless this event, the day has finally come!

06:28.080 --> 06:29.790
We begin with the opening ceremony.

06:30.340 --> 06:33.590
It's time for Kalos Champion Carne-san's opening speech!

06:38.760 --> 06:39.950
Dear Trainers,

06:41.280 --> 06:44.970
the experience and efforts you have accumulated to come here...

06:45.670 --> 06:47.540
...are irreplaceable.

06:48.520 --> 06:53.860
Please feel free to channel all of it into the Kalos League here.

06:56.260 --> 06:57.550
Now then, I hereby...

06:58.080 --> 06:59.540
...declare the Kalos League...

07:00.320 --> 07:01.920
...open!

07:08.690 --> 07:10.690
Fighting in the opening battle will be...

07:10.980 --> 07:12.060
...competitors Trova...

07:12.670 --> 07:14.160
...and Alan!

07:17.870 --> 07:21.090
Until the semifinals, the battles will be three-on-three.

07:21.510 --> 07:24.660
Also, the field will be selected randomly.

07:25.240 --> 07:27.790
All right, the field that will adorn the opening battle is...

07:28.280 --> 07:28.750
...this one!

07:29.860 --> 07:32.240
The water and rock field!

07:36.270 --> 07:38.720
Both of you, please send out your first Pokémon.

07:41.680 --> 07:43.160
Lizardon, I am counting on you!

07:46.510 --> 07:48.800
So Trova's Lizardo has evolved!

07:49.230 --> 07:50.270
What will be Alan's first...?

07:50.690 --> 07:52.110
Come out, Lizardon!

07:57.410 --> 07:59.740
Wow, Alan has picked Lizardon as well!

07:59.960 --> 08:03.790
This is going to be a showdown between two Lizardon! You can't avert your eyes from this!

08:10.800 --> 08:12.060
Out of the two Lizardon,

08:12.330 --> 08:14.110
who will make the first move?

08:15.270 --> 08:17.150
If you are not coming, we will!

08:17.630 --> 08:19.300
Lizardon, Fire Spin!

08:22.590 --> 08:23.130
Dodge!

08:26.990 --> 08:27.640
Flamethrower!

08:29.470 --> 08:30.460
Dragon Claw!

08:37.450 --> 08:39.930
All right, I will play my trump card right from the start!

08:40.230 --> 08:41.350
Let us go, Lizardon!

09:03.430 --> 09:06.280
Trova's Lizardon has mega evolved!

09:06.850 --> 09:07.810
Awesome!

09:07.810 --> 09:11.060
So the trump card he was talking about yesterday was Mega Evolution...

09:11.700 --> 09:12.900
Yeah, surprised?

09:13.610 --> 09:16.190
Trova has been working hard for the Kalos League too.

09:18.120 --> 09:19.960
My Lizardon's Ability is Drought.

09:20.910 --> 09:24.550
It will now deliver Fire type moves that have greatly increased power.

09:25.320 --> 09:25.950
Lizardon,

09:26.270 --> 09:26.940
Heat Wave!

09:30.790 --> 09:31.580
Whirl up some water!

09:35.150 --> 09:37.630
By instantly raising a column of water, it blocked Heat Wave!

09:38.350 --> 09:39.520
I expected nothing less from Alan.

09:40.910 --> 09:42.950
He is making good use of the field.

09:43.150 --> 09:45.340
Lizardon, attack it relentlessly!

09:45.670 --> 09:46.700
Dragon Tail!

09:49.710 --> 09:50.970
Lizardon, evade it!

09:53.800 --> 09:56.670
The entire stadium is heating up!

09:57.390 --> 09:58.570
Let's play for keeps now, too!

09:59.170 --> 10:00.450
Respond to my heart,

10:00.870 --> 10:01.620
Key Stone!

10:02.260 --> 10:03.500
Surpass evolution!

10:04.000 --> 10:05.030
Mega evolve!

10:22.290 --> 10:23.050
There it is!

10:23.510 --> 10:24.930
Alan has now used his, too!

10:25.570 --> 10:28.960
At last, this has turned into a showdown between Mega Lizardon!

10:29.600 --> 10:33.970
Did anyone expect the very first match to become this amazing?

10:36.810 --> 10:37.710
Pokémon Quiz.

10:38.430 --> 10:38.910
The answer is...?

10:40.940 --> 10:50.950
Coming up next:

10:40.940 --> 10:45.910
Two Mega Lizardon clash!

10:41.830 --> 10:46.570
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

10:45.980 --> 10:50.950
Who will make it through the first match!?

10:57.370 --> 10:59.220
Lizardon, Fire Spin!

11:01.670 --> 11:02.660
Flamethrower!

11:07.750 --> 11:11.630
You can't see anything because of the smoke! What's going on in there?!

11:13.510 --> 11:15.480
Lizardon, please fly up!

11:18.430 --> 11:21.310
Oh, Trova's Lizardon couldn't take it any more and fled into the skies!

11:22.890 --> 11:24.560
Fire Flamethrower...

11:25.070 --> 11:26.010
...frontwards at 53 degrees!

11:30.830 --> 11:31.450
Lizardon!

11:39.700 --> 11:42.290
Trova's Lizardon is unable to battle!

11:42.960 --> 11:45.130
Alan's Lizardon wins!

11:48.740 --> 11:49.680
That settled it.

11:50.400 --> 11:55.420
That command is the kind it that is only possible if Pokémon and Trainer share an extremely close bond.

11:56.230 --> 11:57.130
It's so strong...

11:58.590 --> 12:00.770
Hey, Satoshi, you should get going.

12:01.450 --> 12:01.790
Yeah.

12:02.380 --> 12:03.530
Do your best, Satoshi.

12:04.060 --> 12:05.070
You go and nail it!

12:05.740 --> 12:07.130
We will be rooting for you, after all!

12:07.600 --> 12:08.900
Satoshi, go for it!

12:09.300 --> 12:10.780
Yeah, I'm off!

12:21.150 --> 12:22.140
Please come out,

12:22.510 --> 12:23.050
Ptera!

12:27.120 --> 12:29.880
Trova's second is Ptera!

12:32.030 --> 12:33.130
We meet again.

12:34.540 --> 12:35.470
Let's battle.

12:36.020 --> 12:37.320
I have a match right now!

12:37.320 --> 12:38.170
You promised, didn't you?

12:39.510 --> 12:41.190
Sorry, another time, okay?

12:42.810 --> 12:44.020
Are you running away again?

12:46.430 --> 12:48.110
I can't just go around breaking promises.

12:50.190 --> 12:51.280
A promise is a promise.

12:53.990 --> 12:54.990
I gotta keep it!

12:55.520 --> 12:58.500
Now <i>that's</i> what I want to hear from someone with eight badges!

12:59.010 --> 13:01.180
This'll be a no-holds-barred one-on-one match!

13:04.820 --> 13:05.810
Pikachu, I'm counting on you!

13:07.990 --> 13:09.230
What do badges matter anyway?!

13:09.710 --> 13:11.770
I'll prove my strength by defeating you!

13:12.490 --> 13:13.700
Trimmien, Sand Attack!

13:17.710 --> 13:18.430
Oh no!

13:18.720 --> 13:22.670
There are millions of Trainers who don't have all badges but are still strong!

13:23.660 --> 13:24.160
Trimmien,

13:24.530 --> 13:25.810
Giga Impact!

13:28.250 --> 13:29.160
Pikachu, dodge!

13:32.200 --> 13:32.900
Ptera!

13:34.040 --> 13:35.360
Ptera is unable to battle!

13:36.790 --> 13:38.230
Are you all right, Pikachu?

13:40.240 --> 13:41.170
Now, Trimmien!

13:41.620 --> 13:42.200
Take Down!

13:42.980 --> 13:44.510
Pikachu, Iron Tail!

13:49.000 --> 13:50.380
Don't give it time to recover! Electro Ball!

13:51.640 --> 13:53.400
Trimmien, Cotton Guard!

14:01.160 --> 14:01.900
That was close...

14:02.740 --> 14:04.330
You're strong, that's true.

14:05.630 --> 14:08.110
But I'm sorry: I'll win this one and make you let me pass!

14:09.510 --> 14:12.220
It's not like I made it here with half-heated feelings either.

14:13.230 --> 14:16.740
Each and every one of my badges is packed with memories.

14:20.710 --> 14:22.030
I will throw...

14:22.720 --> 14:24.120
...every single bit of them at you!

14:34.900 --> 14:37.770
Mega Lizardon's Flamethrower lands a hit!

14:37.770 --> 14:38.610
Florges!

14:40.000 --> 14:41.430
Florges is unable to battle!

14:41.890 --> 14:43.100
Lizardon wins!

14:43.670 --> 14:44.430
Therefore, the winner is...

14:45.120 --> 14:46.040
...Alan!

14:47.740 --> 14:50.950
The winner of the opening battle is Alan!

14:51.390 --> 14:53.540
He sure showed us the difference in strength between the two.

14:58.450 --> 14:59.590
My time at the Kalos League...

15:00.390 --> 15:01.470
...is over.

15:05.020 --> 15:06.970
We will continue with the second match!

15:08.110 --> 15:11.460
Competitors Tomo and Satoshi will be entering the field!

15:16.790 --> 15:18.280
The battlefield is...

15:19.770 --> 15:21.770
...the meadow field!

15:23.240 --> 15:25.290
O-Oh...? What's going on?

15:25.890 --> 15:28.490
Satoshi hasn't appeared on the field yet!

15:29.010 --> 15:30.150
What?! But why?

15:30.510 --> 15:32.410
Did something happen to him on the way?

15:32.670 --> 15:34.130
What if he doesn't show up?

15:34.580 --> 15:39.230
The opponent wins by default. Satoshi's time at the Kalos League would be over without him even fighting.

15:39.570 --> 15:40.490
What?!

15:41.180 --> 15:43.350
What's that brat boy doing?

15:43.840 --> 15:46.220
He's gonna lose here? Just like that?

15:46.220 --> 15:49.000
It's always in times like <i>these</i> that guy goofs up...

15:51.410 --> 15:53.430
Will Tomo win by default?

15:57.010 --> 15:57.890
Time's up!

15:58.300 --> 15:59.000
Satoshi los-

15:59.000 --> 16:00.010
I'm sorry!

16:00.500 --> 16:01.550
Wait, wait!

16:02.840 --> 16:05.260
Satoshi from Masara Town is here!

16:06.210 --> 16:07.020
It's Satoshi!

16:07.970 --> 16:10.640
Aw, geez... Making us worried like that...!

16:11.060 --> 16:14.070
Can he not at least be ready ahead of time in important moments like this?

16:14.510 --> 16:15.320
There he is.

16:15.560 --> 16:19.200
Oh! Satoshi has finally appeared!

16:19.510 --> 16:21.520
It looks like he's just barely made it in time.

16:25.840 --> 16:26.950
Quick Attack!

16:28.840 --> 16:29.850
Cotton Guard!

16:33.800 --> 16:34.380
It's fast...

16:34.920 --> 16:35.770
Let's finish this!

16:35.770 --> 16:36.880
Thunderbolt!

16:44.420 --> 16:45.070
Trimmien!

16:47.470 --> 16:48.610
Thank you very much.

16:49.980 --> 16:50.760
I lost...

16:57.360 --> 16:59.110
There are plenty of people...

17:02.700 --> 17:03.630
...people like me...

17:04.800 --> 17:08.080
...who're feeling awful because they couldn't collect all their badges.

17:09.410 --> 17:10.900
Honor their dreams...

17:12.180 --> 17:12.760
...their feelings...

17:15.220 --> 17:16.650
Don't lose, no matter what!

17:18.080 --> 17:19.030
Of course I won't.

17:25.310 --> 17:27.180
I'm Satoshi from Masara Town!

17:28.570 --> 17:30.680
My dream is to become a Pokémon Master...

17:30.890 --> 17:31.420
...and...

17:32.620 --> 17:34.580
...to win the Kalos League!

17:36.200 --> 17:38.710
Here comes a declaration of victory!

17:39.150 --> 17:43.660
All right Let's pay close attention to how Satoshi will battle.

17:43.850 --> 17:45.550
Go, Tyltalis!

17:48.800 --> 17:49.800
A Tyltalis, huh...?

17:50.340 --> 17:52.470
Pikachu, you rest for a while.

17:54.690 --> 17:55.330
Gekkouga,

17:55.760 --> 17:57.140
I choose you!

18:00.070 --> 18:01.290
All right, let the second match...

18:01.700 --> 18:02.170
...begin!

18:07.220 --> 18:09.110
Tyltalis, Dragon Pulse!

18:14.500 --> 18:16.700
Dragon Pulse lands a hit on Gekkouga!

18:17.180 --> 18:18.330
Are you all right, Gekkouga?

18:20.290 --> 18:21.830
Tyltalis, Draco Meteor!

18:26.240 --> 18:29.280
Wow, this is a powerful Draco Meteor!

18:29.280 --> 18:30.580
Is it over for Gekkouga?!

18:31.310 --> 18:32.870
Let's bring out all we've got!

18:33.630 --> 18:35.240
Much, much stronger!

18:36.110 --> 18:38.930
Let's go!

18:59.550 --> 19:00.320
Whoa...

19:00.670 --> 19:02.830
So Satoshi had prepared a secret plan as well.

19:02.830 --> 19:04.410
What's that?!

19:04.890 --> 19:07.330
Gekkouga's appearance has changed!

19:07.330 --> 19:08.280
So they've made it their own...

19:08.960 --> 19:09.550
Gekkouga,

19:10.030 --> 19:10.910
Water Shuriken!

19:15.880 --> 19:16.660
Tyltalis!

19:18.760 --> 19:20.420
Tyltalis is unable to battle!

19:20.880 --> 19:22.040
Gekkouga wins!

19:24.110 --> 19:27.530
Satoshi's Gekkouga starts off by claiming one victory!

19:27.780 --> 19:30.690
An outrageous participant has appeared!

19:31.020 --> 19:32.270
You did it, Satoshi!

19:32.270 --> 19:34.760
Satoshi and Gekkouga are so cool!

19:34.760 --> 19:36.100
He still has two left.

19:36.500 --> 19:39.370
All right, let's keep it up and decide the match in one go!

19:41.070 --> 19:43.360
Satoshi, you have finally done it.

19:44.380 --> 19:46.740
The shuriken on its back is a symbol of its power.

19:49.100 --> 19:50.800
But it is not like I have simply been <i>waiting</i> all this time, either.

19:51.930 --> 19:53.630
I will throw everything at you, Satoshi.

20:04.990 --> 20:07.610
The Kalos League has only just begun.

20:08.470 --> 20:11.890
With many different thoughts on his mind, Satoshi progresses through the rounds.

20:12.950 --> 20:16.140
What kind of opponent awaits him next?

20:29.310 --> 20:30.950
Kalos League News

20:31.320 --> 20:35.390
Kalos League News is a special program that will provide detailed information on the Kalos League!

20:35.390 --> 20:37.970
The hosts are me, Takuro - I'm back! - and...

20:37.970 --> 20:39.280
...it's me Yajiko!

20:39.280 --> 20:41.060
No goofing around this time, okay?!

20:41.060 --> 20:41.950
And we'll talk about Ala-baby too!

20:42.170 --> 20:45.970
This tournament is for the top Trainers from all over the country!

20:45.970 --> 20:47.430
Oh wow, there are so many?!

20:47.430 --> 20:51.610
That's right! And the Kalos League is where the strongest of them will be determined!

20:51.610 --> 20:53.020
Oh, wow!

20:51.610 --> 20:52.120
"Is that so?"

20:53.020 --> 20:56.840
Yes, it is so! To stand on this stage, you have to beat eight Gyms, after all!

20:56.840 --> 20:59.980
Wow, that's amazing! The word "strongest" really is lovely though, don't you think?

20:59.980 --> 21:02.590
What are you talking about? You're the strongest in the world of monsters too!

21:02.590 --> 21:05.220
Oh my! You'll get a Rolling Kick for saying that!

21:06.010 --> 21:09.120
Finally, we'll introduce the little hotties that we're keeping our eyes on!

21:09.120 --> 21:09.590
Cute!

21:09.590 --> 21:11.990
Oh my, what a cute and sweet Lizardon-chan!

21:10.310 --> 21:11.200
Cute, so cute!

21:12.030 --> 21:14.220
Isn't it great how they look like a couple with matching outfits?!

21:14.220 --> 21:14.990
Aw, geez!

21:15.160 --> 21:16.260
I want to eat them!

21:16.510 --> 21:20.480
Aw, geez! Paraly-ly-ly-ly-ly-ly-ly-ly-zing!

21:21.080 --> 21:26.070
Sunday July 3rd at 8am!

21:21.820 --> 21:23.870
A field trip to a game company?!

21:23.870 --> 21:25.640
Pokénchi airs on Sundays at 8am!

21:28.210 --> 21:30.120
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.320 --> 21:31.440
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.560 --> 21:33.760
Whoever wins the match between Shota and Tierno...

21:34.680 --> 21:36.610
...will become <i>my</i> opponent!

21:37.270 --> 21:38.510
I cannot lose yet,

21:39.180 --> 21:41.830
...not until I fulfill my promise with Satoshi, until we settle our score.

21:42.280 --> 21:42.860
All right!

21:43.300 --> 21:45.310
We will show you our rhythm!

21:46.200 --> 21:48.750
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:49.030 --> 21:50.890
